Built `compress.py` with a stdlib-only typed encoding for the corpus’s numeric, hexadecimal, and base-36 records, followed by zlib compression; it supports both requested CLI modes. Verified the CLI round trip byte-for-byte. The compressed file is 17,373 bytes versus 44,267 source bytes (60.75% reduction), beating default zlib’s 22,390-byte result. The registered correctness-checked assay passed, and the tested variants did not improve the score.